Client confidentiality (LEG-CONF-03)

Issuer: Advokátska kancelária Hoferová & Bartoš s. r. o. · IČO 51 234 567 · Laurinská 12, 811 01 Bratislava

The duty of confidentiality under §23 of the Advocacy Act (zákon č. 586/2003 Z. z.) covers everything learned in connection with representation, whether or not it is labelled privileged, and it survives the end of the engagement. Only the client can release the advocate from it.
Do not discuss matters in public places, on trains between Bratislava and Košice, or in consumer messaging apps.
Cloud tools require an approved vendor under a data processing agreement; consumer AI assistants must not receive client files.
A police or tax inspection of the office is handled only in the presence of a Slovak Bar Association representative, as the Act requires.
Privilege is asserted, not waived casually in e-mail; document review logs are kept for every production.

